    "introduction": "IMI develops engineering products that control the movement of fluids and gases in industrial systems. Its technologies are used in applications such as process operations, manufacturing automation and building climate control, where precision and reliability can be essential. Customers buy components, systems and related support that help equipment operate safely and efficiently. Revenue comes from original equipment requirements and replacement or service demand across different industrial markets. The business combines engineering design with specialised manufacturing and technical customer relationships. Demand depends on investment and maintenance activity in its end markets, while product performance, energy efficiency and the ability to solve difficult control problems support its competitive position.",
